IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `ea1-part6-contractors`

-- Tests for ea1-part6-contractors.l4 (ss 65 to 66).  Every expected value is written from
-- the text of the section (inputs/EmA1968.txt) before the function was run.
-- Calendar facts used: 1 March 2026 is a Sunday; 29 March 2026 is a Sunday.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 65 Liability of principals, contractors and subcontractors for salary of workman`
-- (1) for the principal: arguments are: the principal contracts with a contractor for labour or work, salary is due to a workman by the contractor or a subcontractor, the contract is for constructional work, the principal is also a constructional contractor.
#ASSERT `s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- constructional work, and the principal is not a constructional contractor: (1B) takes the principal out.
#ASSERT `s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 65(1) "Where a principal ... contracts with a contractor ... and any salary is due": a "Where" not met, no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- for a contractor or subcontractor: the same two conditions, and not the employer.
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is jointly and severally liable with the employer to pay the workman` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is jointly and severally liable with the employer to pay the workman` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 65(1): the same "Where", unmet.
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is jointly and severally liable with the employer to pay the workman` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the salary claimed from the principal` 3000 EQUALS 3000
-- (1A): at most one month's salary.
#ASSERT `s 65(1A) the most a principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is liable for` FALSE 5000 2000 EQUALS JUST 2000
#ASSERT `s 65(1A) the most a principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is liable for` FALSE 1500 2000 EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `s 65(1A) the most a principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is liable for` TRUE 5000 2000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): arguments are: the workman wishes to recover salary from a person liable, a mediation request has been submitted.
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the workman may lodge the claim for the salary under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the workman may lodge the claim for the salary under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the workman may lodge the claim for the salary under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2A): 60 days after 1 March 2026 is Thursday 30 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 65(2A) the last day for submitting the mediation request` (Date 1 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 30 4 2026)
-- if 30 April is a public holiday, Friday 1 May.
#ASSERT `s 65(2A) the last day for submitting the mediation request` (Date 1 3 2026) (LIST Date 30 4 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 5 2026)
-- 60 days after 28 January 2026 is Sunday 29 March, which moves to Monday 30 March.
#ASSERT `s 65(2A) the last day for submitting the mediation request` (Date 28 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 30 3 2026)
-- (2B): the Commissioner may extend the period.
#ASSERT `s 65(2B) the last day for submitting the mediation request as extended` (JUST (Date 30 4 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 5 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 2026)
-- an extension to a day before the original day does not shorten the period.
#ASSERT `s 65(2B) the last day for submitting the mediation request as extended` (JUST (Date 30 4 2026)) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 4 2026)
#ASSERT `s 65(2B) the last day for submitting the mediation request as extended` (JUST (Date 30 4 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 30 4 2026)
#ASSERT `s 65(2B) the last day for submitting the mediation request as extended` NOTHING (JUST (Date 15 5 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: the day the salary became due, the day submitted, the extended day, public holidays.
#ASSERT `s 65(2A) the mediation request was submitted within 60 days after the date on which the salary becomes due for payment` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 65(2A) the mediation request was submitted within 60 days after the date on which the salary becomes due for payment` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(2A) the mediation request was submitted within 60 days after the date on which the salary becomes due for payment` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (JUST (Date 15 5 2026)) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the duty with 60 days: submitted on day 60, fulfilled; on day 61, breached (read both traces).
#TRACE `s 65(2A) the workman's duty to submit the mediation request` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 65(2A) the workman` DOES `s 65(2A) submit the mediation request to the Commissioner` AT 60
#TRACE `s 65(2A) the workman's duty to submit the mediation request` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 65(2A) the workman` DOES `s 65(2A) submit the mediation request to the Commissioner` AT 61
-- (2C): a claim under section 119 lodged before 1 April 2017.
#ASSERT `s 65(2C)(a) subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` TRUE (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(2C)(a) subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` TRUE (Date 1 4 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65(2C)(a) subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` FALSE (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65(2C)(b) the repealed section 65(1C) and (2) as in force immediately before 1 April 2017 continue to apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` TRUE (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 65(2C): "if a workman has lodged, before 1 April 2017, a claim under section 119": a claim lodged on 1 April 2017 is outside the period the text fixes (ruled 2026-11-05 (a)), and a workman who lodged no such claim leaves the "if" unmet.
#ASSERT `s 65(2C)(b) the repealed section 65(1C) and (2) as in force immediately before 1 April 2017 continue to apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` TRUE (Date 1 4 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(2C)(b) the repealed section 65(1C) and (2) as in force immediately before 1 April 2017 continue to apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` FALSE (Date 31 3 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3), (4), (5)
#ASSERT `s 65(3) this section prevents the person from instituting civil proceedings against the employer for the recovery of the salary paid` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(3) this section prevents the person from instituting civil proceedings against the employer for the recovery of the salary paid` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65(4) this section prevents the workman from recovering salary from the employer instead` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(4) this section prevents the workman from recovering salary from the employer instead` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65(5) the person is a principal for the purposes of this section` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 65(5) the person is a principal for the purposes of this section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 66 Registration of contractors and subcontractors`
-- (1): arguments are: the Minister has required registration by notification, the person is registered.
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the person may act as a contractor or a subcontractor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the person may act as a contractor or a subcontractor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the person may act as a contractor or a subcontractor` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 66(1) the person's prohibition on acting as a contractor or subcontractor without registration` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 66(1) the person` DOES `s 66(1) act as a contractor or a subcontractor without being registered` AT 3
-- (2)
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the application for registration is acceptable` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the application for registration is acceptable` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)
#ASSERT `s 66(3) the person is deemed to be the employer of the workmen employed by that person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(3) the person is deemed to be the employer of the workmen employed by that person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): a change of name on Sunday 1 March 2026: the 7th day after is Sunday 8 March, which moves to Monday 9 March.
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the last day for applying for re-registration` (Date 1 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 9 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the last day for applying for re-registration` (Date 2 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 9 3 2026)
-- arguments: registered and changes the name, the day of the change, the day applied, public holidays.
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the application for re-registration was made within 7 days of the change of name` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the application for re-registration was made within 7 days of the change of name` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the application for re-registration was made within 7 days of the change of name` FALSE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 66(4) the contractor's or subcontractor's duty to apply for re-registration` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 66(4) the contractor or subcontractor` DOES `s 66(4) apply in writing to the Commissioner for re-registration and cancellation of the previous registration` AT 7
#TRACE `s 66(4) the contractor's or subcontractor's duty to apply for re-registration` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 66(4) the contractor or subcontractor` DOES `s 66(4) apply in writing to the Commissioner for re-registration and cancellation of the previous registration` AT 8
-- (5), (7)
#ASSERT `s 66(5) the Commissioner may effect the registration of a person and may cancel the registration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(5) the Commissioner may effect the registration of a person and may cancel the registration` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
`a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)` MEANS `Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 1000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING
`a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)` MEANS `Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 2000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the penalty on conviction` (JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) (JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) FALSE EQUALS JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the penalty on conviction` (JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) (JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) TRUE EQUALS JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the penalty on conviction` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Added with the rulings of 2026-11-05: s 66(1) "thereafter a person must not act as a contractor or a subcontractor unless the person is so registered".
-- The prohibition is its own question: it has not begun before the Minister's notification, it applies after it to a person not registered, and the registration lifts it.
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the prohibition on acting as a contractor or a subcontractor without registration applies to the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the prohibition on acting as a contractor or a subcontractor without registration applies to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the prohibition on acting as a contractor or a subcontractor without registration applies to the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 65(1): the person is the employer, so the liability "not being the employer" does not reach the person: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is jointly and severally liable with the employer to pay the workman` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Added with the rulings of 2026-11-05: s 65(1) "where salary is claimed from the principal, this Act (with the exception of section 33 relating to priority of salary) applies".
-- Claimed from the principal: section 33 does not apply, in the Act's own words.
#ASSERT `s 65(1) section 33 relating to priority of salary applies to the salary claimed from the principal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not claimed from the principal: the exception is silent about it.
#ASSERT `s 65(1) section 33 relating to priority of salary applies to the salary claimed from the principal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
